icient—it clears a mid-rank card, doesn\'t overcommit, and allows room for teammate to potentially take control later with similar ranks.\n\nReason: Playing ♠J beats the landlord\'s ♥5 while conserving higher-value cards (A, 2, K, Q) for future critical plays. It avoids flooding the game with a high card unnecessarily and gives my teammate room to maneuver. Since we’re both peasants with large hands, maintaining balance and avoiding premature escalation is key.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠J"]}'}
