ard like the pair of 8s, I avoid taking control unnecessarily and allow my teammate to decide whether to pass or take over with a stronger play.\n\nReason: Playing the pair ♠8 ♣8 is better than using the high single ♣2 because it avoids wasting a top-ranked card early in a free play context. It keeps options open for my teammate to respond with a higher pair or bomb if needed. It also avoids breaking up the pair into a weak single 8. This move maintains balance and cooperation potential.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠8", "♣8"]}'}
